>This may be a stupid question but could someone clarify what
>these phrases mean? I have seen but haven't comprehended.
>Thanks.

Without luckstones, your luck is somewhere between -10 and +10.
After every X moves (where X is a number I don't remember) your
luck changes by 1 towards 0.  (Unless there's a full moon (in which
case it tends towards +1) or a new moon (in which case your luck
tends towards -1))

If you have a cursed luckstone, any good luck will degrade at the 
normal rate, but bad luck will not degarde with time.

If you have an uncursed luckstone (as above) your luck (good or bad)
will not change with time.

With a blessed luckstone, your bad luck improves at the normal rate,
but good luck doesn't degarde with time.  So ideally, you should get
a blessed luckstone, sacrifice or throw gems at unicorns until you're
at max-luck, and then never worry about luck again (unless you do
anything unlucky).

